[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2890901044][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CombatExtended-Continued/CombatExtended/master/Media/Badge_CE_compatible.png[/img][/url] [img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eebette/CombatExtended-SimpleSidearms-Compatibility-Patch/main/Media/Badge_Suite.png[/img] [img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eebette/CombatExtended-SimpleSidearms-Compatibility-Patch/main/Media/Badge_Patch.png[/img]

RimWorld compatibility mod making [url=https://github.com/CombatExtended-Continued/CombatExtended]Combat Extended[/url] and [url=https://github.com/PeteTimesSix/SimpleSidearms]Simple Sidearms[/url] work together.

See [b]My other mods[/b] below for additional modules to create a cohesive game experience while using both CE and SS together.

Inspired by the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3694067502]discontinued mod by Ghosty[/url], I decompiled that mod and searched [i]even harder[/i] for incompatibilities to patch.

[h1]Fixes[/h1]
[list]
[*]Sidearm carry limits now respect CE's inventory system (weight [i]and[/i] bulk).
[*]Weapon ranking uses real CE damage numbers, so pawns actually pick the better gun.
[*]Pawns never auto-switch to a gun that has no ammo.
[*]Enemies spawn with their sidearms loaded and carrying spare ammo.
[*]Switching weapons no longer interrupts a reload partway through.
[*]Drawing a melee sidearm when attacked in melee works again.
[*]Mid-fight auto-switching to a better-suited gun works again.
[*]Firing a single-use launcher leaves the pawn holding their preferred backup, not fists.
[*]When a weapon is destroyed or used up, the replacement follows your sidearm preferences instead of CE's guess.
[*]CE loadout enforcement no longer strips remembered sidearms out of inventories.
[*]EMP and incendiary weapon detection matches the ammo actually loaded.
[*]Melee ranking now accounts for CE armor penetration.
[/list]

[h1]Load order[/h1]
Harmony → Combat Extended → Simple Sidearms → this mod.

